      <h2 id="apropos-context-heading">L'OPÉRATEUR HAS RETURNED WITH TRAINING.</h2>
      <p>Forgotten Industries began as a hardware project during the 2014 enthusiast PC era. It was built from watercooling parts, cases, cables, radiators, fittings, tools, and the obsessive supply chains of a very different internet.</p>
      <p>Over a decade later, in long-term recovery from substance use disorder and after years of scientific, classical, and medical training, he came back to what remained.</p>
      <p>The work had changed. It was no longer only about building machines. It was about recognizing what survived, sorting what matters, documenting what can be known, and giving structure to the things that would otherwise disappear into storage, memory, or waste.</p>
      <p>Forgotten Industries is the continuation of that work: an archive, a workshop, a field log, and a system for preserving the material evidence of a life rebuilt around attention, judgment, and care.</p>
    </div>
